From 2d41ef14fc6e45a4b27784c18d33b8cb72c74dfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jatniel <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:48:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] winit iOS: report a hardware keyboard's keys through
 GameController

UIKit gives key presses to the first responder, and the winit view is that only
while a text field has the on-screen keyboard, so a keyboard folded to an iPad or
paired to a phone reached the game with nothing while playing. GameController
reports the keys of a connected keyboard whatever the view is doing.

game_input.rs listens to GCKeyboard (the one connected now, and any connected
later, with its keys let go when it leaves) and sends KeyboardInput with the
physical key, the key on a US layout, its side, and ModifiersChanged. hid.rs holds
the USB HID usage table (built and tested on every platform).

Text stays the text system's: while the view has the keyboard UIKit sends what is
typed as insertText and deleteBackward, so the keys that write text are left out
then (a key event as well would write them twice), and a release is only sent for
a press that was.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
